| Intentional element identified (literal excerpt)                                                                  | Class    | Justification                                                                                                                         |
| ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| “deliver food from the kitchen to an inpatient room”                                                              | Goal     | This states a desired state of affairs the system should achieve, without fully committing to one specific delivery method.           |
| “The delivery is made on an order-by-order basis in response to kitchen delivery requests”                        | Task     | This specifies a particular operational way of performing food delivery: one order at a time, triggered by kitchen delivery requests. |
| “kitchen delivery requests”                                                                                       | Resource | This is an informational entity needed to trigger delivery; the concern is whether such requests are available to the robot/system.   |
| “The food can be delivered into a room table by the robot”                                                        | Task     | This is a specific way to accomplish food delivery, namely placing the food directly on the room table.                               |
| “requires a special manipulation robot skill”                                                                     | Resource | The manipulation skill is a capability that must be available for the robot to place food on the table.                               |
| “the food can be fetched from the robot's tray”                                                                   | Task     | This is an alternative specific way of completing the delivery, where the meal is taken from the robot tray.                          |
| “requires cooperation with the inpatient, a companion, a nurse, or another robot”                                 | Resource | These cooperating agents are resources because the main concern is whether they are available to help fetch the food.                 |
| “Some inpatients could be unable to fetch the food from the tray”                                                 | Belief   | This is domain knowledge that explains why tray-fetching may not always be feasible and affects design decisions.                     |
| “a companion visitor or nurse could not be available at the moment of the delivery”                               | Belief   | This represents contextual rationale about possible unavailability of human assistance during delivery.                               |
| “information about if the inpatient, a companion visitor or nurse can be able to retrieve the food from the tray” | Resource | This is informational data needed to decide whether tray retrieval is feasible.                                                       |
| “can be obtained based on the inpatient record”                                                                   | Task     | This specifies a particular way to obtain the information needed for deciding whether food can be retrieved from the tray.            |
| “the inpatient record”                                                                                            | Resource | The inpatient record is an informational resource used by the system to determine retrieval capability.                               |
| “information about the patient”                                                                                   | Resource | This is informational data whose availability supports the decision about whether the patient can retrieve food.                      |
| “the presence of a companion into the room”                                                                       | Resource | Companion presence is contextual information needed to determine whether a human helper is available.                                 |
| “This information is subject to uncertainty”                                                                      | Belief   | This is design rationale indicating that the decision-relevant information may be incomplete or unreliable.                           |
| “The robot can carry multiple meals”                                                                              | Belief   | This describes a domain/system assumption that motivates the need to identify the correct meal during retrieval.                      |
| “the robot should indicate which meal should be retrieved by a given inpatient”                                   | Goal     | This states a desired system condition: the correct meal should be identified for the appropriate inpatient.                          |
| “track when and where each meal was retrieved”                                                                    | Goal     | This states a required system outcome: maintaining knowledge of the time and location of each meal retrieval.                         |
| “The robot should alert if a wrong meal is retrieved”                                                             | Goal     | This states a desired system behavior/outcome, detecting and warning about incorrect meal retrieval.                                  |
| “Dirty dishes should be retrieved from the room”                                                                  | Goal     | This describes a desired state of affairs the system should achieve, without specifying only one retrieval method.                    |
| “the dish retrieve can occur unassisted”                                                                          | Task     | This specifies one concrete way to retrieve dishes: without assistance.                                                               |
| “with the cooperation of two robots”                                                                              | Task     | This specifies a particular alternative method for retrieving dishes through robot-robot cooperation.                                 |
| “with the cooperation of robots and a human”                                                                      | Task     | This specifies another particular dish-retrieval method involving human-robot cooperation.                                            |
| “Opening the room door can involve cooperation with another robot or a human”                                     | Task     | This specifies possible operational ways to open the door as part of the mission.                                                     |
| “another robot or a human”                                                                                        | Resource | These are assisting entities whose availability matters for opening the room door.                                                    |
| “Someone in the room can call a robot to pick up the dishes”                                                      | Task     | This specifies a concrete interaction mechanism for initiating dish pickup.                                                           |
| “that person can signal if they can open the door when the robot comes to it”                                     | Task     | This specifies a particular way of communicating door-opening availability to support the robot’s task.                               |

